<title>JAPAN: Japan parliament to debate budget from Jan 27.</title>
<headline>Japan parliament to debate budget from Jan 27.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>A key Japanese parliamentary committee will start debating the supplementary budget for this fiscal year, which ends on March 31, for three days from January 27, a parliamentary official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Ahead of the debate, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka is scheduled to speak to the key budget committee of the Lower House of parliament on Friday to explain the government's supplementary budget and the full state budget for the 1997/98 fiscal year, the official said.</p>
</text>
